+      "verdict": "pass",
+      "evidence": "\"Today a project gets all of the memory and every review runs every rule, so a project with no database, no front end or no permissions still gets those standards and those findings\" \"Initialize starts where that install stops, so a project has no Garura memory of its own until initialize runs, and the two never write the same files.\"",
+      "fix": ""
