++      "verdict": "pass",
++      "evidence": "\"Nothing is made in the tracker and no stand-in is written to the mapping before the product owner's typed yes. A tracker is an outside system, and a new type there, or a work item filed as some other type, is seen by the whole team.\" \"When every needed type is already there, initialize says so and makes nothing, because a second copy of a type would split the team's work items between two types.\" \"that type gets no stand-in and stays unmapped, because a person with the right can still make the real type.\"",
