+++      "id": "self_explanation",
+++      "verdict": "fail",
+++      "evidence": "Most items carry their why (e.g. 'Every read goes through the memory tool, because every part of Garura reads memory that way and the tool is what records where each file came from'; the unreachable rule explains 'An empty result here would look like \"no file fits\"'). Two do not: 'When an answer selects nothing in Phoenix memory (for example a tool memory has no standard for), the record says so in plain words, and the project's memory is built from the other answers. Our default; the sources do not say what happens then.' and 'When a run is repeated (Run initialize again, fn-rerun-initialize), the memory is rebuilt from the new answers, and the record says which files were added and which were taken out.' Also the output 'each with where it came from in Phoenix memory' states no reason for recording the origin.",
