+++      "id": "stranger_test",
+++      "verdict": "fail",
+++      "evidence": "The doc defines Phoenix memory ('the one shared memory on the machine ...') but never says what 'the project's Garura memory' is or where it lives, and its core rule does not say how a file is tied to an answer: 'A memory file is taken only when an answer calls for it. A file that no answer selects stays in Phoenix memory'. The term 'memory blocks' appears in Out of scope ('Keeping each project's memory blocks its own') with no definition here. On a rerun it says the memory is rebuilt but not what happens to the answers already in the profile.",
