++      "fix": ""
++    },
++    {
++      "id": "stranger_test",
++      "verdict": "pass",
++      "evidence": "What: 'After the install, one run of `initialize` sets the project up from the product owner's answers: its memory, its review rule groups and its tracker's work-item types.' Why: 'Today an install copies all of Phoenix memory and a review runs every rule, so a project with no database, no front end or no permissions still gets those standards and those findings, and a play can stop the first time the tracker lacks a work-item type it files.' Edges: the Out lines name the install, the review and work-item filing as other owners, and the Never lines name the hard refusals. Terms such as 'Phoenix memory' and 'rule groups' are not defined, but their meaning can be inferred from how they are used.",
