++- Goal: On a new run each question proposes the earlier answer and names it as its source.
++- Limit: Treat an earlier answer only as a proposal, and make nothing in the tracker before a typed yes.
++- Limit: Never remove a work-item type from the tracker on a re-run.
++- Fails if: a re-run keeps a memory file or rule group that a changed answer rules out.
++- Fails if: a re-run with every answer unchanged changes a memory file, the rule-group record or the tracker.
++- Context: serves the product owner when the project changes; reads the profile's earlier answers and the project as it is now; reuses the first run's features; out is the reinstall.
